{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For many days</b> — without king. And there is no argument from the Hasmoneans, for they are not of the tribe of Judah." "<b>And without sacrifice</b> — Yefet ben Eli said: this is the Tishbite's «to me, for you shall not make for me sacrifice and pillar.» According to his opinion the pillar is not forbidden, only when the Torah speaks of it. But what will he do with the word «terafim»?! And others said: all of it refers to idolatry, and we have not found «ephod» in a derogatory sense." "<b>And the correct view in my eyes:</b> without sacrifice — to HaShem," "<b>nor pillar</b> — to Baal," "<b>without ephod</b> — to HaShem," "<b>and without terafim</b> — to idolatry, for Laban called them his gods."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:00.780094361Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}